{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nCites are on ad630728043 (S6 tip; becomes origin/main when S8 and S6 land).\n\n`dispatch_apply_phases._call_with_retry` (`:76-148`) makes up to 4 attempts on `TimeoutError`, `JiraAPIError` 5xx/429 and raw `HTTPError` 5xx/429. ADR 0103 S3 retires it. Its 15 call sites: update `dispatch_one.py:590` `update_issue`, `:496` `set_parent`, `:683,685` labels; create `dispatch_one.py:242` label, `create_route.py:232` `self._call` (used `:290,297`); links `dispatch_apply_phases.py:542,676`; typed leaves `apply_outbound.py:185,207,232`, `apply_inbound.py:202`, `apply_inbound_events.py:268-269`.\n\nIt nests over transport retry: `acli_rest.py:42-89` (3 attempts on timeout/connection faults, never on `HTTPError`), `acli_subprocess._run_acli` (`:536-666`, 3 attempts on a non-zero exit, not wrapper-retryable), DC `_with_connection_retry` (`jira_datacenter/retry.py:139`, 3 attempts on connection faults; HTTP only for an opted-in 429). A Cloud REST or DC write timeout can reach 4 × 3 = 12 attempts. The coordinator adds no replay: `make_coordinator_dispatch` (`batch_dispatch.py:600-636`) returns only `applied` or `permanent`, and `run_migrated_reroute` passes `budget_factory=None` (`:676`).\n\n`reroute_ordered_create_plans` (`batch_dispatch.py:462-537`) and `reroute_migrated_plans` (`:680-729`) take the planned outbound dicts. The legacy loop (`applier.py:660-666` → `_apply_one` `:703-732`) gets the rest: (a) batches without `ticket_plans`: the `target_mode is None` branch `apply_phase.py:127-136`, which production never takes (`request.py:96-108`, `_lib_ops.py:213`), and 80 test calls in 24 modules; (b) a plan mixing create with non-create, which grouping by target (`ticket_planner.py:283-285`) does not prevent and which stays on the loop (`batch_dispatch.py:694-697`, `test_operation_coordinator.py:1481`).\n\n## Approach\n1. Replace each `_call_with_retry(fn, *a, **k)` with `fn(*a, **k)`, and `self._call(...)` with the direct `self.client` call.\n2. Delete `_call_with_retry`; its imports and re-exports (`dispatch_one.py:53`, `batch_dispatch.py:37,53`, `applier.py:136,321`, `apply_outbound.py:31`, `apply_inbound.py:54`, `apply_inbound_events.py:40`, `create_route.py:232`); imports only it used (`dispatch_apply_phases.py:37,49-54`); `dispatch_one.py:30-36` (unused `import time`, a test patch point). Reword prose: `dispatch_apply_phases.py:6,12`, `dispatch_one.py:2,9,14`, `batch_dispatch.py:5,89`, `applier.py:14,130-132`, `apply_outbound.py:9`, `apply_inbound.py:8,188-189`, `acli_subprocess.py:279-283,563-564`.\n   `RetryExhaustedError` stays public (`acli.py:96`, `applier.py:305`, `batch_dispatch.py:52`); its only raise site, `dispatch_apply_phases.py:146`, goes (`acli_subprocess.py:28` only re-exports it). The guards at `dispatch_one.py:592`, `transition_replay.py:231,261`, `create_route.py:253` stay for other transports; `test_transition_replay.py:645-690` pins them.\n3. Require `ticket_plans` on the batch form: `_typed_batch` (`applier.py:253-265`) raises `TypeError` on `None`, leaving `apply` (complexity baseline 22) unchanged; `_apply_batch` takes it keyword-only and required; `apply_phase.py:127-136` passes `_ticket_plans_kw`. Delete the loop and `_apply_one` (only caller `:666`; `reroute_ordered_create_plans` uses `batch_dispatch._dispatch_with_backstop`, `:515`). The loop becomes `for m in mutations: _record_unrouted(m, ctx, mutations_with_outcomes)`, a new helper that calls `record_backstop_failure(m, LookupError(f\"unrouted mutation: {action}\"), action, ctx)`, appends its outcome and calls `_print_batch_recon(..., soft_failed=True)`; it dispatches nothing, so a leftover dict (case b) is failed, not dropped. Reword `_apply_one` mentions: `applier.py:63,637`, `apply_handlers.py:21,141,146,545`, `batch_dispatch.py:574,587,614,623`, `peer_state.py:105`, `pass_support.py:157`, `docs/architecture.md:548`.\n4. Add a BREAKING section to `docs/release-notes.md` recording ADR 0103 S3 done. Update `docs/code-navigation.md:57-64`, which quotes `_call_with_retry(client.set_entity_property, ...)`, keeping the file names `tests/unit/test_agents_serena_untyped_receiver.py:49-57` asserts.\n\nBREAKING: handlers make one attempt. Retry left in a pass: Cloud REST timeouts and connection faults, ACLI non-zero exits (3 attempts each), DC connection faults and opted-in 429. HTTP 429/5xx on a Cloud REST leg (`set_parent`, `set_entity_property`, `update_issue`'s transition/priority) or any DC write is not retried, reverting story 9622 (`test_retry_httperror.py:1-5`). A non-404 `HTTPError` is fail-fast (`batch_dispatch.py:571-581`), so one 5xx on `update_issue` aborts the pass; so does one on the inbound-create write-back (`apply_inbound_events.py:268-269`; the inbound loop `applier.py:440-460` has no backstop). On a label, link or parent sub-op it counts failed. The next pass re-diffs.\n\n## Scope\nSource: `src/rebar/reconciler/{dispatch_apply_phases,dispatch_one,create_route,apply_outbound,apply_inbound,apply_inbound_events,batch_dispatch,applier,apply_phase,apply_handlers,peer_state,pass_support}.py`, `adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py` (docstrings).\nTests (in `tests/unit/reconciler/` unless rooted):\n- Delete `apply/test_applier_retry.py`, `test_timeout_s_forwarding_heldout_7504.py`.\n- Drop wrapper tests: `test_retry_httperror.py` (keep `:41-52,104-119`), `test_retry_after_zero_guard_heldout.py:55-102`, `test_cloud_rate_limit_sweep_heldout.py:139-184` (docstring `:3-5`), `test_error_taxonomy.py:46-64`, `apply/test_apply_handlers_operation_outcome.py:58-73`.\n- Rewrite to one attempt: `apply/test_applier_identity_write.py:135-212`, `apply/test_applier_stale_binding_404.py:193-212`, `apply/test_applier_clean_label.py:43-65`, `mutate/test_operation_coordinator.py:1441-1480`.\n- `test_transport_port_completeness_heldout.py:154-162` still passes but stops proving value-form detection (both members become calls); feed it a parsed snippet.\n- Step 3: the 24 modules in the file impact pass plans from `ticket_planner.plan_pass` (no new `tests/_*.py`, which the mechanism ratchet counts); `apply/test_handler_404_isolation.py`, `test_dc_outbound_status_routing_5200.py`, `test_live_mode_failure_tally.py:656-690` stop calling `_apply_one`.\n- Unchanged: 9 modules naming it only in prose or a negative assert (e.g. `mutate/test_coordinator_route_census.py:241`).\nDocs: `docs/release-notes.md`, `docs/code-navigation.md`, `docs/architecture.md`.\nUnchanged: no env var or config key is read (fixed `max_retries=3`); no ratchet baseline names removed code; ADR 0055:235 and 0084:34 stay historical. Out of scope: transport retry loops, `retry_budget`, the coordinator.\n\n## Testing\nHappy: `make verify`; `pytest tests/unit/reconciler tests/unit/test_agents_serena_untyped_receiver.py -q`. Edge: (1) through `run_migrated_reroute`, a transport whose `update_issue` raises `HTTPError(503)` once then succeeds is called once, the raw 503 propagates, nothing sleeps (today: 2 calls, applied); (2) a 404 on update still soft-fails (`apply/test_applier_stale_binding_404.py:104`); (3) a 503 on `set_entity_property` after create: one call, no `delete_issue`, identity alert written; (4) `TimeoutError` from `create_issue` still yields `CreateSignal(status=\"timeout\")` (`create_route.py:250-254`); (5) a mixed create/non-create plan's dicts are recorded failed, not dispatched; (6) batch `apply` without `ticket_plans` raises `TypeError`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `_call_with_retry` absent from `src/`: `git grep -n '_call_with_retry' -- src` prints nothing.\n- [ ] A transient 503 on update reaches the transport once per pass (no handler retry, no coordinator replay) and propagates as the raw `HTTPError` — edge test 1.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` prints `new=0`.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] `make verify` exits 0.\n  provenance: environment=local dev host; principal=Rebar Bot Nava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — run log on the ticket"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1792656639152999001,"uuid":"b6fc4c97-e0d0-4ceb-aba5-ea9a50656cb1"}